  "text": "URGENT: Cross-patient data visibility during medication substitution alert\n\nI am writing because we had a serious incident involving medication substitution alerts. Earlier today, while trying to handle an out-of-stock pharmacy notification, a screen popped up that appeared to display another patient's active medication history and pharmacy profile instead of the chart I was working in. Our staff caught it quickly, but we are extremely concerned about a potential data privacy leak between records. I have locked the terminal and noted the exact time this occurred. We need an urgent review of how these substitution workflows pull up patient context to ensure this does not happen again."
